-## 4. Build, test and deployment configuration
-
-| ID | Severity | Finding | Fix |
-|---|---|---|---|
-| D1 | High | **No CI at all** — `gh api .../actions/workflows` returns `total_count: 0`. Nothing prevents another broken build from reaching `main`. | Add `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: install (with cache), build, Cypress. |
-| D2 | Medium | **No `test` script**, so `npm test` fails and Cypress is only invoked by the Netlify plugin. | `"test": "cypress run"`, plus `"test:e2e:dev": "cypress open"`. |
-| D3 | Medium | **Cypress `baseUrl` mismatch:** `cypress.config.js` points at `http://localhost:8888`, while `npm run dev` serves `http://localhost:3000`. Tests only work under `netlify dev`, which is not documented. | Set `baseUrl` to `http://localhost:3000` or add a `dev:netlify` script and document it. |
-| D4 | Medium | **The only test asserts template text** ("Welcome to my app!"), so it will pass on any deployment of the untouched starter and proves nothing about real content. | Replace with tests for the routes/content you actually ship, or delete. |
-| D5 | Medium | **`netlify.toml` is minimal and unpinned:** `publish = ".next"` (correct only because Netlify auto-installs the Next runtime), no `[[headers]]`, no Node pin, `netlify-plugin-cypress` with no `inputs` (defaults to running only on deploy previews). | Pin `@netlify/plugin-nextjs` version, add `NODE_VERSION`, add security headers (see §6). |
-| D6 | Low | **`next export` script is vestigial** and conflicts conceptually with `.next` publishing; nothing uses it. | Remove. |
-| D7 | Low | **Node version unpinned** (`engines`/`.nvmrc` absent). Next 12 + Node 22 is an untested combination; Netlify's default Node image changes over time. | Pin to Node 20 (12.x is not validated on 22). |
-
-**Deployment status evidence:** the live site `https://stunning-choux-0e728c.netlify.app` responds with the starter page, but every Netlify check on PR #1 fails:
-
-```
-Header rules - stunning-choux-0e728c        fail
-Pages changed - stunning-choux-0e728c       fail
-Redirect rules - stunning-choux-0e728c      fail
-netlify/stunning-choux-0e728c/deploy-preview fail
-```
-
-Treat HEAD as broken in CI; confirm in the Netlify UI whether production is serving a stale deploy.
